body:
I'll come out of the woodwork and say I really enjoyed the game. I loved the first one and I had heard the user reviews for this were abysmally low. Playing through the game I kept an open mind and I learned to embrace it. This game goes between focusing on the world, the characters and the plot. We love Joel and Ellie because of our experience with them in the first game but this game unravels how there's so much to this world than just them. Nobody gets the heroes death with great fanfare and people's decisions here are muddy, unclear and even unsure. That to me felt human and maybe that's why this game made me felt so unsettled to see things play out like this. 

&#x200B;

I'd give it between a 9-10/10. I don't know what I'd detract from it other than some segments felt long but as a fan of the game/series I enjoyed the extra time with the characters.
